@startuml
title Typed Access to a Value - Redis-like Server

' How a command reaches a value (SDD 6.3, DX-DT-2, DX-DT-3). A command never
' sees a value of the wrong type: the lookup either gives the right type,
' nothing, or a WrongType failure that the command turns into an error reply.
' Strings use find_string / find_or_create_string, which work the same way.

start
:A command (HSET, LPUSH, HGET, SREM ...)
looks up its key by name;

if (Command writes a new collection?\n(HSET, LPUSH, RPUSH, SADD, APPEND)) then (yes)
  :find_or_create<T>(key)
  (find_or_create_string for APPEND);
else (no)
  :find_as<T>(key)
  (find_string for string reads);
endif

:find(key): a key past its deadline\nis erased and looks missing;

if (Key exists?) then (no)
  if (find_or_create?) then (yes)
    :Create an empty T under the key;
    :Return the new value;
  else (no)
    :Return nullptr;
    :Read commands reply as for an empty value
    (nil, 0, empty array);
    stop
  endif
else (yes)
  if (Value is of type T?) then (yes)
    :Return the value;
  else (no)
    :Return the WrongType failure;
    :Reply "WRONGTYPE Operation against a key\nholding the wrong kind of value";
    note right
      MGET is the exception: it replies nil
      for a key of another type, as Redis does.
    end note
    stop
  endif
endif

:The command reads or changes the value;

if (Command removes elements?\n(LPOP, RPOP, HDEL, SREM, SPOP)) then (yes)
  :erase_if_empty(key);
  if (List, set or hash now empty?) then (yes)
    :Erase the key and its deadline;
  endif
endif
:Reply;

stop
@enduml
